# .claudeignore — agent read exclusions for the `ant` model-metadata cache.
#
# Rationale (D-17 / ANT-04): the `ant` enrichment cache stores model metadata at
#   ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/claudia-statusline/ant/models.json
# Agents browsing this repository should not ingest a cache directory if one ever
# appears *inside the project tree* — for example when the test suite points
# XDG_CACHE_HOME at an isolated directory under the repo. The globs below exclude
# any such in-tree ant cache (directory and contents) from agent reads.
#
# HONEST SCOPE NOTE: a repository-root .claudeignore can only govern paths inside
# this repository. It CANNOT and DOES NOT protect the real user-home cache at
# ~/.cache/claudia-statusline/ant/ (or the macOS ~/Library/Caches equivalent),
# which lives OUTSIDE the repo and is therefore outside this file's reach. The
# actual defense-in-depth for the real cache is structural, not this ignore file:
#   1. The cache struct (src/ant/cache.rs) stores NO API key / secret field.
#   2. The Admin/standard key is never logged or written to the cache (Plan 03).
# This file is in-tree-test-cache hygiene only — do not read it as a guarantee
# about files under the user's home directory.

# In-tree ant model-metadata cache (e.g. tests with an isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME)
**/claudia-statusline/ant/
**/claudia-statusline/ant/**
**/claudia-statusline/ant/models.json

# In-tree ant PRICE cache written by `ant sync-pricing` (PRICE-04, Phase 11).
# Same in-tree hygiene scope as above. The synced price table carries no
# credential field and the fetch that produces it is keyless by construction
# (D-01), so this is tidiness rather than secret protection.
**/claudia-statusline/ant/prices.json
